{"id":"gen-1780882822-yBakXHN4W4EdC3DaP1eg","object":"chat.completion","created":1780882822,"model":"openai/gpt-5.5-20260423","provider":"OpenAI","system_fingerprint":null,"service_tier":"default","choices":[{"index":0,"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"tool_calls","native_finish_reason":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":null,"refusal":null,"reasoning":"**Deciding on Monopoly strategy**\n\nI've just had a trade rejected, so now I'm considering my options. I have $109 in cash. I can build on the pink properties, as I have 4 houses available. Upgrading those to hotels would return the houses to the bank. Building a hotel costs $100 and could raise rent significantly. It seems like a good move, especially since it might also allow Claude to build on his light blue properties due to released houses.**Analyzing Monopoly strategy**\n\nClaude has four houses on his light blue properties and can build hotels for $50 each without needing additional houses. Since he can't add houses to mortgaged properties, releasing houses doesn\u2019t impact him much. However, if he unmortgages his red properties, he might build a monopoly. The risk is low liquidity, but building a hotel on Virginia for $100 will still leave me with $9 cash. Overall, I think I'm well-positioned with my developed greens.**Evaluating house strategy**\n\nI need to consider whether to maintain a house shortage. Building a hotel releases houses, but only Claude can potentially add to his light blues since he already has four houses. Those can be converted to hotels without needing additional houses. Releasing four houses doesn't matter much for his build options. Keeping no hotels on pink ties up houses, which prevents Gemini from developing the dark blues that require bank houses to build. So, less urgency in keeping a house lock.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","index":0,"id":"call_auVKNybmU4Rry7gN0bAoFb07","function":{"name":"propose_trade","arguments":"{\"offer\":{\"cash\":0,\"properties\":[],\"get_out_of_jail_cards\":1},\"request\":{\"cash\":75,\"properties\":[],\"get_out_of_jail_cards\":0},\"to_player_id\":\"Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview\",\"public_message\":\"Gemini, separate from the dark blues: $75 for my Get Out of Jail card. It keeps you moving and liquid enough to choose your own timing instead of getting stuck.\",\"private_thought\":\"Try to convert the jail card into cash buffer. If Gemini accepts, he has less cash for dark-blue development and I gain liquidity; card also keeps him moving into my rents instead of camping jail.\"}"}}],"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.summary","summary":"**Deciding on Monopoly strategy**\n\nI've just had a trade rejected, so now I'm considering my options. I have $109 in cash. I can build on the pink properties, as I have 4 houses available. Upgrading those to hotels would return the houses to the bank. Building a hotel costs $100 and could raise rent significantly. It seems like a good move, especially since it might also allow Claude to build on his light blue properties due to released houses.**Analyzing Monopoly strategy**\n\nClaude has four houses on his light blue properties and can build hotels for $50 each without needing additional houses. Since he can't add houses to mortgaged properties, releasing houses doesn\u2019t impact him much. However, if he unmortgages his red properties, he might build a monopoly. The risk is low liquidity, but building a hotel on Virginia for $100 will still leave me with $9 cash. Overall, I think I'm well-positioned with my developed greens.**Evaluating house strategy**\n\nI need to consider whether to maintain a house shortage. Building a hotel releases houses, but only Claude can potentially add to his light blues since he already has four houses. Those can be converted to hotels without needing additional houses. Releasing four houses doesn't matter much for his build options. Keeping no hotels on pink ties up houses, which prevents Gemini from developing the dark blues that require bank houses to build. So, less urgency in keeping a house lock.","format":"openai-responses-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.encrypted","data":"gAAAAABqJh2m47EK9SFLVu2sGF9hNX2KIJ2OiHrd-wVAlAX6DqWS9lBrpOKrMN2JIkAbT6mmh2pchyhRiv86SKgoy7VJyF-JKG6vxFBLmCiXAzrWufxlNYN_-M7y32K4bOn_KV1jMCKzlqk_7NfusfPpCwrwWOjwIHqS3NlOUw_jqNLRN4MBU4BrQZbVAaqhKkwy5ER5CcrIlsvkfAl1lUwVnNrifQuzLgFalkf7CAnc9hCd1eg8UxYaEEkoVGhMkxg4gnM9W7ikkPPE9hDUMklHolHdwSJoRkUJuRnSyouSTUyDHuqYqwgIWEbYJqnXvZMYSNA1GVjSpM45rWoFGw8sshc1OeVZIFto-29jnm-EBd5_1KEZH1AlKsP-YZ3V1aEOJpwUdk3Kvav_n3z-8mOb473lWAQy6_hYoUuicFB8OTyt0LnzThbXjzmIClolQId8JUyGm1nZJsuWKVNuRsVZtevFgaMczOgz5KN7O9Z8lWjU9FrOUGzKj8I4wnWnOsu8P8fwv9msiEtjDG2DBG4pN61uh1RiX2flesnLfg_Ka-qMyHIcKWByB11AQatJ8uj1BP8T9m_3IntRaxAOhxxm79rjV3kASniFlUBZaOV5W5XmbCNc_WVuNSt_pCZfK7pxVGSAD61CxAqESlrIZJOK-LFd0tkvQ0zUvxQES0RttVg88x_tvIvKL9Ye4fFSslvHXUHGsRU3_doDDguAgVDeWV01_AK6aTNNNPc64So3D84Kxsq7zB4TDMUaAX2Y4JpqMH8aw-sOY46TDo9Uyv88RfiDMe-nnTKgl1EfjJzlLoVS7gwKKpFiOyQF3atgvcUTdJcsptENsXwibgoAcJzlbeBLzb1LeeA9XQLumrSJtTlevf7Kp247_D-hr7PZxEg0b8SlourehzQXq8fIVnhI9G2R60mbvz9pHe1qc6qJpaBPTPK3LLqnxcE6p5jZdds6gbJphwygpx5a95GGVaIBNH-_xTd--kSxo9dJ4YIO5O1Kcqjs1b0DuffYMk1f-FJmFr9GowACFhXbK2WBAMcrMwOsP3kyrpG0GvAH7iCfqOtFsdOMIrJyHxv7jvT-f73ead_fZnQafGZNARcs4dQ7PM2ypCHKk_c0Blpuz7g6dEy0P7Nvju2xP1o05LMNnDuvvpbj-V_e4DMYXvThQe6z0ugCojMDkMue26BjNbw2RA1TBnb6z5S77TCna697j5ryxX7a2Heeqh8a3DtPhquicDDf7wODCv8uCdfUM3ZdiB-TUvo-80fbjmc-qrFDkNBEabb4VhMTBIQExsMMm8Lp2G2e1ZBd_o3LtqU57uOBf7ih8wSpKBSXEWC9nrtPUwH6iyEVgwOVzmiKU3Z3dC8faPlHgyISef2ba1TSEOOjjg9Iwo_AWfNOVJh3LpRFE-OUtufZy2qdfHORNvG2NnpWva_DgJ5xCLtpZwDcqDpX1_PxMRx_b6xvSDYVwQgHitHv4aFvSGzkIqKFFy93dp8qcktGeh0-v4VwgjyAhAe5Dy4gY67LH0rQtxK0wAD55mg3m37C84apSj3VZw6clOhfOFFOCG5zOECBK3mtqZ0k2W2_l3oHY1iB54cUFD8tcn37yq8fjRQ77apnpRdztD0i9y3cQvOYMoIXBPSATOAhRu9pyVMk2jtPl_EuUV_BVsNzd0FctQfyLZpf-A-BU-c4h0t7VkmjzLxWiHzk-_8rD9uJU2xIODRllDMOqij2erPC9L9P42V1VoH9QMgOsJdzv56EDfWUk9OeMTNXKRVnGzwvopf6YauAj-QgmafSq7mUxeKtPOvTlf8YrzQs28qlSX33epvCP0q_EvpQYPTg9-B2